 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did 1492 begin with a surrender and a broken promise?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In Granada, the last Muslim kingdom in Spain. Its surrender came with a promise that did not last."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How much was left of al-Andalus by then?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1491",
   "place": "Granada"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Only Granada, after nearly eight centuries. Castile and Aragon, now ruled together by Isabella and Ferdinand, held the rest of Spain."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "By 1491, the city was under siege.",
   "scene": "alhambra",
   "date": "1491",
   "place": "Granada",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did they fight to the end?",
   "scene": "boabdil",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "No. The sultan, Boabdil, negotiated. Muslims could keep their mosques, their laws, their faith. Isabella and Ferdinand signed."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "On the second of January 1492, Boabdil handed over the keys of the city.",
   "scene": "granada2",
   "date": "2 January 1492",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Legend says he looked back from a mountain pass and wept. That spot is still called the Moor's Last Sigh.",
   "scene": "suspiro",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And the map?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1492",
   "place": "Spain"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "For the first time since 711, no Muslim state was left in Spain."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And the broken promise?",
   "scene": "expulsion",
   "date": "31 March 1492",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Three months later, the same monarchs signed the Alhambra Decree. Spain's Jews had four months: convert, or leave."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Tens of thousands left homes their families had lived in for over a thousand years. Many found refuge in the Ottoman Empire.",
   "scene": "sephardim",
   "date": "1492",
   "place": "Mediterranean"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Their descendants, the Sephardim, still speak Ladino, a form of old Spanish.",
   "scene": "expulsion2",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And Granada's Muslims?",
   "scene": "alhambra2",
   "date": "1502",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Within ten years, they too were told: convert, or leave."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Columbus, and the land he never understood. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "scene": "granada",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: Columbus, and the land he never understood",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ],
